WEBVTT

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:16.910
Witch...

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.390
You don't suppose it was Amon who hunted Kate, do you?

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:30.830
Amon...

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:40.630
In the end, are you, too, nothing but an offspring of Saturn?

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.580
I don't think we will meet again.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:19.670
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:25.400
...the instant I look away.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.540
I just kept counting...

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:35.980
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:43.350
...that I'd vomited up.

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:49.290
In this time that seems so dry,

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:54.400
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:02:00.260
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:03.310
...and tears them to pieces.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:12.980
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:20.810
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.700
I'm sorry.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:12.150
What the hell has that guy been looking at all morning?!

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.810
If you've got no business here, get lost!

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.510
I'll call the cops if you don't beat it!

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.120
What was that all about?

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:53.690
Yes, I've heard.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.570
For the love of... You people never do what you're told.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:04:00.600
This office isn't some flophouse, you understand me?

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:03.910
But Robin was attacked!

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:07.580
I'm aware of that. But she doesn't have to stay HERE.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:10.350
The last thing I need is you people getting the rest of us involved.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.380
You must be joking!

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.620
In any case, this is something you people did on your own.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.350
Leave me out of it.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.060
Way to dodge that responsibility, boss.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:26.420
Hey, do you know what happened to the food that I left sitting here?

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:31.030
Speaking of food, we need to get Robin some breakfast!

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:32.930
Right, I totally forgot about that.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:35.910
Looks like she's doing okay fending for herself.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:46.280
Maybe we're worrying ourselves over nothing.

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:47.520
Yeah...

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.270
Attack the STN-J?!

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:02.530
Wait a minute, I wasn't informed of any such decision!

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:09.080
Very well. In any case, just give me a little more time.

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:10.970
Right.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:22.550
Using that bullet as a starting point, I was able to narrow it down to these three.

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:24.520
But this is as far as I can go.

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:26.160
Why?

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:31.000
These three are classified as the top class of all hunters.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:36.560
Their files have some nasty protection on them, so I can't dig down any further.

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:39.630
But all you need now is more data?

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:42.210
It's nothing that major.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:47.950
If I could just figure out if any of these three had entered Japan recently...

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.880
Oh, is that all you need?

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.250
How far back would you like me to go?

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:57.090
Well, two or three years should do it...

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.620
But not even headquarters could get you any information on hunters...

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:02.230
Oh, it's me, Kosaka.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.930
I hate to bother you, but could I speak to Takahashi...

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:07.060
...over in criminal investigations #2?

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:11.540
You people might not give much credit to the Japanese police, but I...

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:14.170
Oh, is that you, Takahashi?

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:16.000
Yeah, it's me.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:18.150
Sorry to call you out of the blue,

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:20.770
...but I was wondering if you could do some digging for me.

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:25.420
Yeah, something like that.

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:28.790
Intensive Care Ward

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:28.860
This morning?

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:34.260
Yes, sir. It wasn't during normal visiting hours, but he insisted.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:36.860
Right this way.

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:42.130
He didn't mention his name, did he?

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:43.870
No, sir...

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:47.770
But he was very tall, and a bit dangerous looking.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:52.440
Should I not have let him in, sir?

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:55.680
No, it's fine. Thank you.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:57.540
Of course.

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:05.180
Amon...

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:32.850
You must hate me.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:37.990
I can't do a single thing for you as a father.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.280
Oh, right... That letter.

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:09.050
I guess there's no way to get it right now.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:14.320
It's me.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:18.490
Fine. I'll look the other way this one time.

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:22.290
But whatever happens, the STN-J isn't to be...

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.740
Is this the one?

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:34.080
His name and face are different, but yeah, the DNA is a match.

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:39.150
Evgeny Kitaenko. Born in St. Petersburg, Republic of Russia.

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:42.180
Entered Japan two years ago, and that's all they know.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.390
Two years... I wonder if he's still around.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:49.360
There are no records of him leaving the country, so it's pretty safe to assume that.

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:51.900
But can we trace his movements?

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:55.830
I thought I told you never to underestimate the power of the police.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:57.800
Just leave it to me.

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:02.840
I know all the guys who handle illegal immigrants like this.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:06.010
Can you track those guys down right away?

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:08.810
Well, I suppose so...

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:10.520
Then please get to it.

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:14.580
We have to track him down before he makes his next move.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:20.690
Karasuma and Sakaki, you should stay here. We have to keep watch over Robin, too.

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:22.390
- S-Sure.
- Okay...

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:24.470
C'mon, now.

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:27.830
Chief, I'm gonna need that sharp tongue of yours.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:37.270
Virgo for today..."Watch out for guests wearing black," huh?

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:47.750
Miss Robin, you're safe here. Your guest is waiting for you.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:06.240
I heard what happened from Amon, so I thought I'd drop by and check on you.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:07.930
You talked to Amon?

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:12.880
Touko is apparently still in a coma.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:17.980
But he said to tell you not to worry, and that she's sure to make a full recovery.

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:23.720
I'm sorry...

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:28.630
But I just can't understand Amon.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:35.060
That's no good.

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:38.900
When you lose faith in people, you can't do your best.

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:43.230
Listen to me. Mr. Amon is a man you can trust.

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:45.970
He would never betray anyone.

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:49.040
So have faith in him.

00:10:55.720 --> 00:11:00.290
And now, here is a special lunch that I made to cheer you up. I outdid myself this time.

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:06.690
Go eat up while it's still warm.

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:34.180
Hey, Michael? It's me.

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:40.230
It's from Miss Dojima.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:41.730
Yeah...

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:44.270
I knew it!

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:45.530
And?

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:48.630
What? He was killed?

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:53.810
Wait, are you saying he was killed two years ago, right after he entered the country?

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:56.620
Yeah, there's no doubt about it.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:12:02.150
I looked at the postmortem reports, too, but it matched the forensic DNA data.

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:04.850
But if he's dead, what the hell...

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:11.090
Michael, there was one other person who could use that bullet, right?

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:12.790
One other?

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:14.390
Amon.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:16.330
Yeah, but...

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:19.970
No way, that's just not possible.

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:21.810
Why would Amon do that?

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:26.140
I'm not really sure. I've been thinking about it since it happened.

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:31.020
Maybe we've been averting our eyes from the truth.

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:36.490
It's an undeniable fact that Kate was hunted by someone close to us.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:39.150
Who was it, then?

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:41.890
No!

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:43.460
That can't be true!

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:44.760
Why not?

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:48.330
How can you be so sure?

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:53.540
I understand why you'd want to believe that.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:56.510
But then, where has Amon gone?

00:12:57.140 --> 00:13:01.010
At a time like this, nobody's so much as seen him since yesterday.

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:02.840
But...

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:04.980
But that doesn't mean...

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:12.420
Um, Chief, about this receipt...

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:01.710
Worm to Intruder.

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:04.510
Target nerves secured.

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:07.280
Security system completely offline.

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:11.350
Intruder here, roger that. Will now commence operation.

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:14.550
Good luck. Meet you topside.

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:45.880
Who is it?

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:03.540
You sons of...!

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:15.620
Aw, man...

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:17.240
Do you have his known associates?

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:20.620
Give me a minute!

00:15:21.090 --> 00:15:22.680
I'll give you another three seconds.

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:33.570
That's not the car's fault...

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:37.030
Oh, are you saying that I'm just a bad driver?

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:38.840
I didn't say that.

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:40.260
Yes, you did.

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:52.750
Look, getting back to the matter at hand...

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:53.690
Want some coffee?

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:56.250
What happened just before Kitaenko was killed?

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:59.230
It's right here, see it?

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:02.230
- Do you want some fresh coffee?
- So it's just a matter of efficiency.

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:04.700
- Y- Yeah, sure...
- You use too much energy to do the job.

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:31.720
Robin! Get out of here!

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:37.160
Dammit!

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:38.990
Michael!

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:40.990
Come with me.

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:54.260
No good. Secure the exit!

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:55.540
Hurry!

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:07.750
What the hell?!

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.360
Amon...

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.830
They're here to hunt you.

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:22.160
They've decided that your powers are dangerous.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:25.060
Dangerous?

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:31.840
But why are you helping me, Amon?

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:36.170
Come with me!

00:18:37.150 --> 00:18:42.380
Amon, are you the one who hunted the person I replaced?

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:45.990
That's right. I hunted Kate.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:50.430
She tried to smuggle out the secrets of the STN-J.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:52.630
Solely to satisfy her own greed.

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:54.630
No, that's not right.

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:59.630
She betrayed us to escape from herself.

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:04.310
Kate had known, even while she was losing her mental balance.

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:09.510
She knew that she had lost control of her power, the power of her Craft,

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:13.980
...which meant that she herself would be hunted as a Witch some day.

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:18.920
At some point, she developed a death wish when she could no longer cope with that fear.

00:19:20.730 --> 00:19:23.860
But hunting your own partner...

00:19:29.470 --> 00:19:33.770
There was no trust as partners between the two of us.

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:36.440
There was only...

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:41.680
They've broken through?

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:45.110
Come on, hurry!

00:19:49.090 --> 00:19:51.990
Robin, can you blast a hole through that wall?

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:54.260
I can do it, but...

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:55.490
Do it.

00:19:57.600 --> 00:19:58.790
All right.

00:20:12.050 --> 00:20:16.920
Amon, you believed in me...

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:25.220
I was ordered by Zaizen to not interfere with your hunt.

00:20:26.060 --> 00:20:28.720
But I couldn't do it.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:33.530
Amon, I...

00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:38.610
Let's go!

00:20:39.410 --> 00:20:40.370
This way!

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:49.610
Robin, I don't think you're a Witch.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:56.990
Get moving.

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:07.100
What about the others?

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:08.500
Don't worry about them.

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:10.900
Hurry!

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:28.250
Listen, if anything happens to me, go to this man for help.

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:34.920
A-Amon!

00:21:35.900 --> 00:21:36.860
Go!

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:39.390
Why?

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:42.760
Robin, go down those stairs and take the underground passage!

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:46.160
No way! If you stay here, Amon, you'll...

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:50.600
Stop that! Just go!

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:01.020
Robin, the next time I see you...

00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:33.080
Is this the last of them?

00:22:33.650 --> 00:22:35.390
Looks like one got away.

00:22:35.390 --> 00:22:36.750
We'll look for the girl later.

00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:40.760
Contact Squad 2 and tell them the building is completely secured.

00:22:44.900 --> 00:22:46.060
Amon...

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:49.130
Amon...

00:22:57.410 --> 00:22:58.740
Amon...

00:23:00.610 --> 00:23:01.910
Amon...

00:23:07.090 --> 00:23:09.750
We'll secure the server's hard drive right away.

00:23:09.890 --> 00:23:12.220
Hurry up and get switched over to backup power.

00:23:12.930 --> 00:23:14.920
We've already seized the samples.

00:23:15.830 --> 00:23:18.570
The database probably has a protection program...

00:23:18.570 --> 00:23:20.430
...that will automatically destroy its contents.

00:23:20.430 --> 00:23:21.700
All external links have been severed.

00:23:21.700 --> 00:23:23.570
Please don't touch it until we get there.

00:23:23.570 --> 00:23:26.270
The building's system is now running in a standalone state.

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:28.670
I'd like to continue with the operation.

00:23:29.080 --> 00:23:31.640
Please override the security system password.

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:35.440
I'll ask. But for now, good work.

00:23:35.780 --> 00:23:37.890
I'm just glad none of your team got hurt.

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:39.180
Thank you, sir.

00:23:42.860 --> 00:23:46.850
This wasn't a hunt...?
